      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CHARMING PERIOD HOUSE, SET IN A TRULY UNIQUE SETTING WITH THE BREATHTAKING GLENART CASTLE/BALLYRAINE MIDDLE WOODLANDS IN THE BACK DROP.  THE PROPRTY WAS ORIGINALLY CONSRUCTED IN C. 1874 AND WAS EXTENDED AND COMPLETELY REFURBISHED IN 2008.  THIS BEAUTIFUL HOME CONSISTS OF C. 184 M² 3 BEDROOMS AND 3 BATHROOMS AND SITS ON C.0.28 OF AN ACRE OF BEAUTIFUL GROUNDS."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR ACCOMMODATION\r\n\r\nLIVING ROOM  (4.025M X 6.878M)\t\t\r\nLiving Room with a red brick tv wall housing a mulberry solid stove with granite hearth. Exposed granite walls\r\nwith ceiling coving and a mix of tiled and solid flooring.  Stairs to first floor with under stairs storage, and open \r\nthrough to Kitchen.\r\n\r\nKITCHEN/DINING ROOM   (3.442M X 5.263M)\t\r\nWith a bespoke fully fitted cream kitchen incorporating a Belfast sink and granite work top counters and fired earth tiled splash backs.  Inset Rangemaster stove with extractor fan, full height tiled splashback and overhead pelmet.  Integrated appliances include a Normende dishwasher and fridge.  Bespoke built in welch dresser.  Tiled floor, tiled splash backs and door through to Utility Room, and through to Formal Dining Room.\r\n\r\nFORMAL DINING ROOM   (3.419M X 3.308M) + (0.809M X 2.90M)\r\nWith laminate flooring and dual aspect windows, one being a large Bay.  Double doors leading out onto decked patio area.  Vaulted, timber ceiling.\r\n\r\nUTILITY ROOM   (2.095M X 1.938M)\t\r\nWith tiled flooring and door to side of property.\r\n\r\nWC   (1.145M X 1.881M)\r\nWith white suite WC & WHB.  Stone mosaic tiled floor, tiled walls with stone mosaic feature.    \r\n\r\nSITTING ROOM  (6.920M X 3.868M) + (0.809M X 2.9M) + (0.809M X 2.9M)\t\r\nGenerously sized carpeted room, located to the side of the property running the full width of the property.  With \r\ndual aspect windows, two large Bays and a beautiful feature marble open fireplace.  Arched doorway leading out to the side of the house.\t \t \r\n\r\nFIRST FLOOR ACCOMMODATION\r\n\r\nLANDING   (1.834M X 2.828M) + (1.149M X 4.940M)\r\nCarpeted stairs and landing with recessed spot lighting and chandelier. \r\n\r\nMAIN BEDROOM 1   (3.536M X 6.900M)\t\t\r\nSpacious main bedroom with laminate flooring and three dual aspect windows and a velux.\r\n\r\nEN-SUITE   (0.887M X 2.570M)\t\t \t\r\nWith white suite WC, WHB & built in tiled shower unit (Triton T90xr electric shower).  Velux window.  Mosaic flooring.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 2   (2.696M X 3.841M) + (0.753M X 1.581M)\t\t\t\r\nDouble room to the front with laminate flooring and velux window.\r\n\r\nSTORAGE CUPBOARD   (1.580M X 1.059M)\r\nWith lino flooring and built in shelving.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 3    (2.950M X 3.860M) + (0.456 X 1.570M)\t\t \t\r\nLocated to the rear of the house with laminate flooring, Velux window and location of access to attic.  Stone mosaic\r\ntiled flooring.\r\n\r\nMAIN BATHROOM   (2.570M X 2.050M)\t\t\t\t\r\nFully tiled with free standing bath, wc and whb.  Shaver light point over sink.  Storage cupboard.\r\n\r\nGARDENS\r\nThe property stands on approximately C. 0.28 Acre of magical surrounding mature gardens.  Boasting lovely\r\nmanicured lawns and meandering stone pathways leading to a decked area which sits close by to the babbling \r\nBallyduff stream which lies on the southern boundary of the property.  There are mature bedding, shrubbery and trees set throughout these spacious grounds. There is a further raised decked and fenced patio area to the side of the property.  A white picket fence borders off the rear garden, which is the location of a lovely tree house and a C. 20 M² garden shed.  To the front is a gravelled parking, and ample space for a further outside entertaining area.  Ornate granite steps leading up to the front door which leads you through to this highly impressive home. \r\nGENERAL\r\nLocation is second to none, this picturesque private home is set just off the R.747 (Vale Road), C. 3 Km west of Arklow Town’s Upper Main Street. To the rear of East Gate Lodge sits the beautiful mixed forestry of Ballyraine Middle Woodland which merge into Glenart Woods and its walkways which are located close by.  This charming period home is truly unique in not just by way of its location but in the way this bespoke property has been lovingly presented, styled and maintained by the current owner.  The property offers generous and versatile accommodation over two floors, and boasts all the convenience of modern living which creates a really special family friendly home.\r\nThe private surrounding gardens are lovingly laid out and landscaped,  making an ideal space for outdoor living \r\nand alfresco dining.  \r\n \r\nSERVICES\r\nESB – Mains, Water – Own Well & Sewerage – Septic Tank.\r\nWindows & Doors – Hardwood double glazing throughout and hardwood front door.\r\nHeating System –  Oil Fired Central Heading (Under Floor) and Solid Fuel Stove & Open Fireplaces.\r\nBER –  C2  (BER Number: 119442697)"
      },
